      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Georg Thieme Verlag KG Stuttgart · New York.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
            "Label": "BACKGROUND",
            "content": "Various combinations of bony and soft tissue anomalies have been described at the craniovertebral junction (CVJ). These include posterior fossa dermoids (with or without dermal sinuses) associated with Klippel-Feil anomalies and dermoids (no previous reports of overlying dermal sinuses) associated with bony anomalies."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "PATIENTS",
            "content": "Two patients with a combination of CVJ anomalies are described."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "Both patients had a posterior fossa dermoid, dermal sinus, and occipitalized C1 arch. Furthermore, one patient had a complex bony CVJ anomaly, and the other had a Klippel-Feil anomaly in addition. The clinical presentation and management are elucidated."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "content": "Patients who present with any one of these lesions need to be evaluated for the existence of other congenital anomalies. These are complex malformations to treat."
          }
        ]
      },
